{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpine column definitions commonly contain strings or functions that return HTML strings for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":". The rendering utilities resolve those definitions with the correct table context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the recommended table-aware wrapper. Pass exactly one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<template x-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n  <th>\n    <span x-show=\"!header.isPlaceholder\" x-html=\"FlexRender({ header })\"></span>\n  </th>\n</template>\n\n<template x-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n  <td x-html=\"FlexRender({ cell })\"></td>\n</template>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/alpine-table"},{"type":"text","value":" and expose it to the Alpine data scope, or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" on a table created by the adapter. For footer groups, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender({ footer: header })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function for a definition and context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRender } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It invokes function renderers and passes non-functions through unchanged. It does not select grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-html"},{"type":"text","value":" inserts HTML, only render markup produced by code you trust. Escape or sanitize untrusted data before including it in a renderer result. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-text"},{"type":"text","value":" or normal DOM bindings instead when a renderer only needs to display text."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders that placeholder."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nAlpine column definitions commonly contain strings or functions that return HTML strings for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. The rendering utilities resolve those definitions with the correct table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended table-aware wrapper. Pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```html\n<template x-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n  <th>\n    <span x-show=\"!header.isPlaceholder\" x-html=\"FlexRender({ header })\"></span>\n  </th>\n</template>\n\n<template x-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n  <td x-html=\"FlexRender({ cell })\"></td>\n</template>\n```\n\nImport `FlexRender` from `@tanstack/alpine-table` and expose it to the Alpine data scope, or use `table.FlexRender` on a table created by the adapter. For footer groups, call `FlexRender({ footer: header })`.\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and returns `null` for grouping placeholders.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a definition and context:\n\n```ts\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt invokes function renderers and passes non-functions through unchanged. It does not select grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders.\n\nBecause `x-html` inserts HTML, only render markup produced by code you trust. Escape or sanitize untrusted data before including it in a renderer result. Use `x-text` or normal DOM bindings instead when a renderer only needs to display text.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders that placeholder.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Alpine) Guide\n---\n\nAlpine column definitions commonly contain strings or functions that return HTML strings for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. The rendering utilities resolve those definitions with the correct table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended table-aware wrapper. Pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```html\n<template x-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n  <th>\n    <span x-show=\"!header.isPlaceholder\" x-html=\"FlexRender({ header })\"></span>\n  </th>\n</template>\n\n<template x-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n  <td x-html=\"FlexRender({ cell })\"></td>\n</template>\n```\n\nImport `FlexRender` from `@tanstack/alpine-table` and expose it to the Alpine data scope, or use `table.FlexRender` on a table created by the adapter. For footer groups, call `FlexRender({ footer: header })`.\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and returns `null` for grouping placeholders.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a definition and context:\n\n```ts\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt invokes function renderers and passes non-functions through unchanged. It does not select grouped-cell renderers or suppress grouping placeholders.\n\nBecause `x-html` inserts HTML, only render markup produced by code you trust. Escape or sanitize untrusted data before including it in a renderer result. Use `x-text` or normal DOM bindings instead when a renderer only needs to display text.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders that placeholder.\n"}
